  "failure_history": [
    "Final deployment review found the private Compose URL rejected by the new URL policy. Exact explicit HTTP origins and Compose/Helm configuration were added; only the affected original Go top and the integrated actual journey were repeated. Disk-full infrastructure attempt ran zero origin subcases; original receipts retained.",
    "Initial Go generation/consumer attempts encountered the concurrent queryTypedIndex dependency gap; no behavioral cases ran and no placeholder was substituted.",
    "Initial native infrastructure attempt encountered cached pnpm junction resolution and ran zero behavioral cases. Existing installed real package targets were linked; no dependency installation.",
    "Native domain/tombstone top passed in a command whose sibling used an over-specific lexical-first RRF rank assertion. Only the sibling was corrected and rechecked; individual unchanged results were reused, not called a whole-package pass.",
    "Control temporarily reverted a shared provider-error guard to demonstrate its HTTP regression, then restored and accepted the final guard. This was not an isolated overlay; original receipts are retained. No Root actual journey was active during that temporary change.",
    "Two confirmed read-path fixes require current authority even on a provider error and bind returned sequence to the exact local publication event.",
    "Owner final source review found late asynchronous save after unlock and a normal32-budget obstruction of explicit authorized rebuild recovery; both were corrected together and only affected checks recompiled/retested."
  ],
